-\end{enumerate}
+\subsection*{Further consequences and refinements}
+
+\paragraph{The exact MF residual of $E$.}
+Put $B=\iota(\mathcal B)$, $d=\hat c=tct^{-1}$ and
+$D=\langle\!\langle u\rangle\!\rangle_E$, where $u=[d,v_1]$.  Then
+\begin{equation}\label{eq:exact-mf-residual}
+ \operatorname{Res}_{\mathrm{MF}}(E)
+ =D=N_{\mathrm{conj}},
+ \qquad
+ E/D\cong \Sigma *_B(B\times C_2),
+\end{equation}
+and $E/D$ is MF.  If
+$q\colon E\to E/\langle w\rangle$ is the quotient map, set
+$\bar B=q(B)$, $\bar t=q(t)$ and
+$D_{\mathrm{coll}}=D_{\mathrm{coll}}(\bar B,\bar t)$.  Then
+\[
+ \operatorname{Res}_{\mathrm{MF}}(E/\langle w\rangle)
+ =D_{\mathrm{coll}}=D/\langle w\rangle,
+ \qquad
+ \operatorname{Res}_{\mathrm{MF}}(E)=q^{-1}(D_{\mathrm{coll}}).
+\]
 
